==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|lamp|ing|lang=en}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# A form of [[hunting]], at [[night]], in which bright lights or [[lamp]]s are used to [[dazzle]] the hunted [[animal]] or to attract insects for capture.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{label|en|archaic}} [[bright|Bright]], [[flashing]], [[resplendent]].
#* '''1590''', {{w|Edmund Spenser}}, ''The Faerie Queene'', III.3:
#*: Most sacred fire, that burnest mightily / In liuing brests, ykindled first aboue, / Emongst th'eternall spheres and lamping sky [...]!

